Done. `enqueueMany(newItems)` in `src/queue.js` checks `items.length + newItems.length > capacity` up front and throws `QueueFullError` before touching the array, so overflow leaves size, head, and contents untouched; otherwise it appends in order and returns the new size (which is why an empty array naturally returns the current size). Three tests added in `test/queue.test.js` cover success ordering, atomic overflow, and the empty no-op — `node --test` is 31/31 green, and only those two files are modified.
